{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DescentNodeExists","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphyYoung"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.murphyM_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.murphyM_smul","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyGarnirFactor.lean#L264-L280","doc":"**`m_{s, w • g} = m_{s, g} · T_w`** on a length-additive factorisation.\n\nThis is the Murphy-element form of `Tw_dAt_smul`, and the step 3.14's induction rewrites\nwith.  Nothing is assumed about `g` being Garnir — the lemma is exactly as strong as its\nlength hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.exists_garnir_Tw_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.exists_garnir_Tw_factor","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyGarnirFactor.lean#L224-L253","doc":"**Mathas 3.13, lifted to the `T`-basis.**\n\nA row-standard non-standard tableau's `T_{d(t)}` factors as `T_{d(g)} · T_w` for a Garnir\ntableau `g`.  Both halves come from elsewhere — the descent node from\n`exists_garnir_length_additive`, the lift from `Tw_dOf_smul` — and this is where they meet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.smul_eq_of_dOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.smul_eq_of_dOf","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyGarnirFactor.lean#L215-L220","doc":"**The `w` that carries one tableau to another.**  `d` is a bijection onto `S_n`, so\n`t = w • g` has a unique solution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.invSet_toFinSucc_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.invSet_toFinSucc_mono","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyGarnirFactor.lean#L193-L211","doc":"Inversion-set containment survives the re-indexing `Fin (nOf μ) ≃ Fin (n+1)`.\n\nNeeded because `exists_garnir_length_additive` states its containment over `Fin (nOf μ)`\nwhile `length_dOf_smul_eq_add_iff` wants it over `Fin (n+1)`, where the Coxeter system\nlives.  The content is that `finCongr` preserves `Fin.val`, hence the order, hence which\npairs are inversions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.Tw_dAt_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.Tw_dAt_smul","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyGarnirFactor.lean#L169-L181","doc":"The same lift for the **column**-superstandard reference, in the `dAt` form `murphyM`\nconsumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.Tw_dOf_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.Tw_dOf_smul","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyGarnirFactor.lean#L152-L167","doc":"**`T_{d(w • g)} = T_{d(g)} · T_w`** when the lengths add — the row-superstandard\n(Mathas) reference.\n\nThe hypothesis is exactly the conclusion of `length_dOf_smul_eq_add_iff`, so a Garnir\ndescent node feeds it directly (§3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.dAt_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.dAt_smul","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyGarnirFactor.lean#L137-L145","doc":"The same, transported to `Fin (n+1)` where the Coxeter system lives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.HeckeMurphyYoung_dOf_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor.HeckeMurphyYoung_dOf_smul","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyGarnirFactor.lean#L127-L135","doc":"**`d(w • g) = w · d(g)` for the column-superstandard reference.**  The companion of\n`TableauPerm.dOf_smul`, which proves it for the row-superstandard one. ","signatureChunk":0}]}